WEBVTT

00:32.430 --> 00:37.040
It wasn't a dream, then?

00:38.010 --> 00:49.860
<b><i>Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World</i></b>

02:09.170 --> 02:12.490
<i>Dragonians are a proud race, with a destiny.</i>

02:13.030 --> 02:17.820
<i>Their destiny is to serve the human who
will become the hero, and save the world.</i>

02:20.270 --> 02:23.120
You can hold them in your hands
for a better look, miss.

02:29.570 --> 02:31.150
How much is this?

02:31.150 --> 02:32.540
20,000 dinah.

02:34.050 --> 02:34.990
20,000...

02:35.370 --> 02:37.970
Sorry. No discounts.

02:44.750 --> 02:46.500
Wh-What's wrong?

02:46.500 --> 02:50.020
You're a Dragonian! You need to be careful!

02:50.420 --> 02:53.490
I can't sell it, now that it's damaged.

02:53.490 --> 02:55.230
I didn't do it!

02:55.230 --> 02:56.500
It wasn't me!

02:56.500 --> 02:58.270
It's okay to be careless, occasionally.

02:58.270 --> 03:01.000
But it's not nice to lie.

03:01.000 --> 03:02.650
B-But...

03:02.650 --> 03:05.610
You look like you just came out
of the backwoods,

03:05.610 --> 03:08.830
but here in the Labyrinth City,
we take these things seriously.

03:10.820 --> 03:14.550
I'm not a monster.
I know you didn't mean it.

03:15.790 --> 03:18.310
I'll let it slide if you
buy it for half price.

03:18.310 --> 03:22.120
Or would you rather we take
this to the Solar Knights?

03:23.350 --> 03:27.110
I told you to talk to me when
you go shopping, Curran.

03:27.830 --> 03:29.160
Calios!

03:29.820 --> 03:35.240
That Dragonian girl ruined
a 20,000 dinah pendant!

03:35.930 --> 03:37.810
I can't sell it now...

03:37.810 --> 03:39.730
C-Calios...

03:39.730 --> 03:41.670
Try scratching this pendant.

03:43.060 --> 03:45.230
Wh-What?!

03:45.230 --> 03:47.490
You can't sell it anyway, right?

03:47.490 --> 03:49.910
So who cares what she does with it?

03:49.910 --> 03:54.000
That's only if I get my 10,000 dinah!

03:54.000 --> 03:55.550
Sure, I'll pay for it.

03:56.190 --> 03:58.530
You know what'll happen
if I do, though, right?

03:59.820 --> 04:01.180
Just try it.

04:17.110 --> 04:19.650
Can you make a smaller scratch on it?

04:19.650 --> 04:21.580
N-No.

04:22.980 --> 04:24.330
You heard the lady.

04:24.910 --> 04:28.120
You were likely trying to foist damaged
goods on her, but you picked the wrong girl.

04:28.460 --> 04:30.740
I-It's got nothing to do with you!

04:30.740 --> 04:32.600
I'm the one who paid the money.

04:32.600 --> 04:34.240
Wh-What are you doing?!

04:35.980 --> 04:37.720
It's an old con.

04:38.500 --> 04:43.290
He swapped it for the damaged pendant,
to make it look like you'd done it.

04:44.130 --> 04:48.920
So, you wanted to take this
to the Solar Knights, right?

04:48.920 --> 04:51.010
No, well...

04:51.010 --> 04:53.980
Curran, do you want this pendant?

04:53.980 --> 04:55.490
Y-Yes...

04:55.910 --> 04:58.640
I'm taking this in exchange
for not turning you in.

04:58.640 --> 05:01.180
And you'll give me back the
gold piece I just gave you.

05:01.180 --> 05:02.430
Damn it!

05:04.190 --> 05:05.130
Here you go.

05:09.550 --> 05:11.010
Calios...

05:13.090 --> 05:16.070
<i>Dragonians are a proud race, with a destiny.</i>

05:16.070 --> 05:20.770
<i>Their destiny is to serve the human who
will become the hero, and save the world.</i>

05:21.670 --> 05:26.110
<i>I believed that it was him. I worshiped
him and gave him everything I had.</i>

05:27.150 --> 05:32.200
<i>I believed in him completely. And every
day I spent with him was wonderful.</i>

05:47.600 --> 05:49.170
Are you ready, Curran?

05:50.210 --> 05:52.250
What's all that gear?

05:52.250 --> 05:55.020
You won't be able to beat our foe
today without light equipment.

05:55.020 --> 05:56.690
But...

05:58.390 --> 06:03.040
Nobody's brave enough to
try and steal from <i>you</i>!

06:03.040 --> 06:07.190
And we'll be coming back alive,
no matter what, right?

06:08.550 --> 06:09.450
Yeah.

06:10.010 --> 06:11.220
You're right.

06:11.680 --> 06:15.390
<i>Ten years after the war,
with the world at peace,</i>

06:15.390 --> 06:19.620
<i>I was so lucky to meet
someone I could serve.</i>

06:20.100 --> 06:21.820
Fire Dragon Strike!

06:29.780 --> 06:32.460
Amazing, Curran! You're incredible!

06:32.460 --> 06:34.460
You're even stronger than S-rank!

06:36.090 --> 06:38.340
Well done, Curran!

06:46.520 --> 06:49.410
You sure I don't have to help?

06:49.410 --> 06:52.850
Don't take any more of our jobs, okay?

06:52.850 --> 06:53.750
You've got that right!

06:55.970 --> 06:58.860
That's the right thing to say.
I'm happy you feel that way.

06:59.400 --> 07:03.780
But an adventurer has to trust their party.

07:04.230 --> 07:06.380
Yes, but...

07:06.890 --> 07:09.660
If you're not good at something,
leave it to somebody else.

07:09.660 --> 07:12.180
Just do the things you're good at.

07:14.910 --> 07:16.990
I'm counting on you, Curran.

07:17.600 --> 07:20.640
Of course! Leave it to me, Calios!

07:24.100 --> 07:26.470
We're almost to the pot snake.

07:27.050 --> 07:31.570
It's wary, and if it hides in its pot,
magic won't work on it.

07:32.270 --> 07:35.510
But if you smash into its pot,
it'll get angry and come out.

07:35.510 --> 07:37.300
That's where you come in!

07:37.560 --> 07:39.850
Of course, it'll attack whoever comes at it.

07:39.850 --> 07:42.370
But we'll do everything
we can to protect you.

07:42.370 --> 07:43.900
Believe in us!

07:43.900 --> 07:46.510
Okay! Leave it to me, Calios!

08:04.080 --> 08:05.460
Great, Curran!

08:05.820 --> 08:06.830
Thanks!

08:15.600 --> 08:17.820
Okay, back her up!

08:29.530 --> 08:31.740
Calios, what's that?!

08:31.740 --> 08:33.170
It's just trying to scare you!

08:33.170 --> 08:34.230
Stay focused!

08:34.230 --> 08:36.210
We'll get ready to deal the killing blow!

08:36.210 --> 08:37.570
Keep it occupied!

08:37.570 --> 08:39.620
O-Okay!

08:44.240 --> 08:46.370
Calios, are you ready yet?

08:49.430 --> 08:50.880
Calios!

08:57.340 --> 08:59.620
Calios, help...

09:10.540 --> 09:15.780
It builds up powerful poison in its body
that it will unleash in emergencies.

09:15.780 --> 09:18.190
But after that, it becomes temporarily weak.

09:22.810 --> 09:25.520
Which means we can handle
the rest on our own.

09:25.520 --> 09:27.510
Thank you, Curran.

09:27.510 --> 09:30.450
Wh-Why?

09:30.450 --> 09:33.150
She's still talking!

09:33.150 --> 09:36.700
Dragonians are a scary race. They're tough.

09:37.090 --> 09:39.890
Now, let's get what we came for and go home!

09:41.680 --> 09:42.940
Help me...

09:43.530 --> 09:45.230
Calios!

09:45.690 --> 09:48.160
I can't hold it all!

09:48.160 --> 09:51.660
Wait, Calios!

10:06.040 --> 10:07.880
<i>The Dragon King's Jewel...</i>

10:08.790 --> 10:10.240
<i>I need it back...</i>

10:11.110 --> 10:15.320
I used the finest materials and spent
a year empowering it with magic.

10:15.320 --> 10:20.320
It will stay with you your whole life,
and grow alongside you.

10:20.320 --> 10:23.760
<i>I need to protect it...</i>

10:33.940 --> 10:36.790
Weren't you with Calios?

10:36.790 --> 10:37.650
She came back?

10:37.650 --> 10:39.010
She's alive?

10:39.010 --> 10:40.660
I can't believe it!

10:42.270 --> 10:45.050
Wh-Where's Calios?

10:45.550 --> 10:47.360
Um... well...

10:49.220 --> 10:53.160
He said you died in the labyrinth.

10:54.370 --> 10:55.500
My things!

10:55.500 --> 10:57.300
Where are my things?!

10:57.300 --> 11:01.680
Calios said something about sending
them back to your family!

11:06.150 --> 11:08.300
I'm counting on you, Curran.

11:56.520 --> 11:57.820
Food...

11:59.170 --> 12:00.550
Maybe I should eat.

12:05.180 --> 12:07.720
Is this enough?

12:10.030 --> 12:11.460
Excuse me.

12:21.520 --> 12:23.000
Welcome!

12:25.780 --> 12:27.890
One pork ginger plate.

12:27.890 --> 12:28.710
Sure thing!

12:29.130 --> 12:31.080
Hey, isn't that...

12:31.080 --> 12:34.010
Yeah, it's him!
Fifs, the Solo Eater!

12:36.000 --> 12:37.400
Fifs...

12:37.400 --> 12:38.520
Here you go!

12:57.120 --> 12:58.890
He's so cool!

13:00.790 --> 13:02.330
Welcome!

13:06.590 --> 13:08.760
One pork ginger plate.

13:08.760 --> 13:11.450
Okay, chef, whip up another
pork ginger plate!

13:11.450 --> 13:17.200
<i>After that, I would hear people talking about
him every time I came into the restaurant.</i>

13:17.570 --> 13:22.060
<i>He was so strong that the guild let
him go into the labyrinths solo.</i>

13:22.630 --> 13:26.330
<i>His registered party name
was "The Solo Eater".</i>

13:26.330 --> 13:30.100
<i>They all called him Fifs, the Solo Eater.</i>

13:52.520 --> 13:54.240
Yum!

14:14.120 --> 14:15.000
<b>Ã€ la carte</b>

14:14.160 --> 14:15.750
<b>Beetlemania Stew</b>

14:14.160 --> 14:15.750
<b>Jellied Jell-Jell Tortoise</b>

14:14.160 --> 14:15.750
<b>Trial-By-Fire Tarwhine</b>

14:14.160 --> 14:15.750
<b>Seafood Skewers</b>

14:14.160 --> 14:15.750
<b>Lamb Skewers</b>

14:14.160 --> 14:15.750
<b>Water Dragon Baked in Oven</b>

14:14.160 --> 14:15.750
<b>Soups</b>

14:22.300 --> 14:27.240
I always say that you've gotta
try this place's lamb skewers.

14:28.010 --> 14:31.930
<b>Beetlemania Stew</b>

14:28.010 --> 14:31.930
<b>Jellied Jell-Jell Tortoise</b>

14:28.010 --> 14:31.930
<b>Trial-By-Fire Tarwhine</b>

14:28.010 --> 14:31.930
<b>Seafood Skewers</b>

14:28.010 --> 14:31.930
<b>Lamb Skewers</b>

14:28.010 --> 14:31.930
<b>Water Dragon Baked in Oven</b>

14:28.010 --> 14:31.930
<b>Soups</b>

14:28.240 --> 14:32.970
Oh, and don't forget the
stewed beef and beets soup.

14:31.930 --> 14:35.890
<b>Egg (Chicken, Quail, Lizard)</b>

14:31.930 --> 14:35.890
<b>Infinite Wakame</b>

14:31.930 --> 14:35.890
<b>Glorious Doppleganger Mushroom Soup</b>

14:31.930 --> 14:35.890
<b>Stewed Beef & Beets</b>

14:31.930 --> 14:35.890
<b>Hellswallow's Soup</b>

14:31.930 --> 14:35.890
<b>Daily Market Price</b>

14:32.970 --> 14:35.890
Yes, the one that's the second
from the bottom on the menu!

14:58.270 --> 15:00.650
I guess it's time to get a new coat!

15:00.990 --> 15:05.340
It wouldn't do to visit a fancy
restaurant in a dirty coat!

15:21.060 --> 15:24.480
Oh, yeah, the bathroom's over there.

15:28.170 --> 15:29.690
That's my life.

15:34.250 --> 15:37.140
Thanks. I should've been more careful.

15:37.140 --> 15:38.210
N...

15:38.210 --> 15:40.020
N-No, thank you!

15:42.200 --> 15:44.960
The food here's just too good.
That's my problem.

15:45.180 --> 15:48.710
I'd recommend the shrimp
and mushrooms in olive oil,

15:48.710 --> 15:51.180
but I'll try that next time I come by.

15:54.730 --> 15:57.110
<i>No, thank you, Fifs.</i>

15:57.110 --> 16:01.290
<i>You taught me a lot about
how to enjoy good food.</i>

16:04.430 --> 16:07.100
<i>That was the last time I saw Fifs.</i>

16:07.410 --> 16:11.870
<i>From what I heard, he's somewhere
out there in the labyrinths.</i>

16:13.130 --> 16:16.730
<i>Being betrayed and stolen from
opened a hole in my heart.</i>

16:16.730 --> 16:19.060
<i>And delicious food did
a good job filling it.</i>

16:23.150 --> 16:26.750
<i>Which meant my new enemy would be food.</i>

16:26.750 --> 16:29.050
<i>Good food costs money.</i>

16:29.670 --> 16:32.340
<i>And I needed to make money.</i>

16:44.470 --> 16:45.640
This one's...

16:46.430 --> 16:48.790
No, it's more...

16:50.260 --> 16:52.310
No, I think it was smaller...

16:53.690 --> 16:58.220
Why didn't she get mad back then?

17:00.420 --> 17:03.060
<i>The fact that she didn't
just makes it scarier...</i>

17:03.060 --> 17:04.720
It's the stray dog!

17:04.720 --> 17:05.910
Don't call me that!

17:06.460 --> 17:10.200
Oh, you're not quite as
stray as you were before.

17:10.200 --> 17:12.140
A-Ah... Agaâ€”

17:14.720 --> 17:18.050
You don't think that means
she really doesn't care?

17:18.050 --> 17:22.120
Yeah, but she might be really
mad and not showing it.

17:22.120 --> 17:25.520
But how would you or anybody else know?

17:25.520 --> 17:27.970
True, but...

17:28.640 --> 17:33.460
Why not ask her where they
sell it or something?

17:33.460 --> 17:35.420
You're acting like it's not your problem...

17:35.420 --> 17:36.740
It's not.

17:36.740 --> 17:38.170
True.

17:38.540 --> 17:39.810
You're being selfish.

17:40.940 --> 17:43.230
You don't care what she thinks.

17:43.230 --> 17:46.430
You want to apologize by
giving her something.

17:46.430 --> 17:48.890
That's selfish, isn't it?

17:49.560 --> 17:52.470
But I think that's okay.

17:52.470 --> 17:57.590
I'm sure the reason I talked to you
that day was that I'm selfish, too.

17:57.590 --> 18:01.360
If you're not going to be able to
move on until this is dealt with,

18:01.360 --> 18:03.990
then why not just be selfish?

18:04.440 --> 18:07.360
That's one way to put it.

18:07.360 --> 18:10.280
Your gift to her should be you, yourself.

18:11.040 --> 18:13.770
Me, myself?

18:25.900 --> 18:27.210
That looks good!

18:28.210 --> 18:31.010
Nick! This is happonyaki!

18:31.780 --> 18:36.330
It's little balls of fried flour with
chopped up eight-legs inside it!

18:36.330 --> 18:37.050
Here!

18:43.410 --> 18:44.650
That's what everybody does!

18:44.650 --> 18:47.160
My throat's burning so bad,
I could breathe fire!

18:47.160 --> 18:49.550
You sure this isn't just for Dragonians?

18:49.550 --> 18:50.970
Maybe it is!

18:51.710 --> 18:55.190
Oh, and the little floaty
things on top are alive.

18:55.190 --> 18:58.060
Make sure you chew thoroughly or
they'll eat you from the inside out!

18:58.400 --> 19:00.820
I already swallowed it!

19:03.170 --> 19:04.660
<i>She's laughing so cheerfully...</i>

19:05.190 --> 19:07.680
<i>This must be who Curran is, normally.</i>

19:10.480 --> 19:13.950
Do you like birds, Curran?

19:13.950 --> 19:15.230
I do.

19:15.230 --> 19:16.800
Y-You do?

19:16.800 --> 19:19.580
With sauce, or with salt!

19:19.580 --> 19:21.430
Especially with that crispy skin.

19:21.430 --> 19:26.190
No, I mean like, swans...

19:26.970 --> 19:31.190
I don't know, 'cause I've never had one.

19:31.190 --> 19:33.700
But as much as anybody, I guess?

19:34.280 --> 19:35.670
As much as anybody...

19:35.670 --> 19:40.540
Listen, you really don't need
to worry about that pendant.

19:40.540 --> 19:41.810
But...

19:41.810 --> 19:45.820
I'm a lot better off this way.

19:48.030 --> 19:51.450
I'm a lot better off this way.

19:53.450 --> 19:54.950
Oh.

19:55.590 --> 19:56.730
Nick.

19:57.650 --> 19:58.840
It's going to get cold.

19:59.640 --> 20:00.790
Oh.

20:01.510 --> 20:02.880
Aah!

20:03.500 --> 20:05.590
It's burning hot!

20:08.300 --> 20:10.080
Hey, Survivors!

20:10.080 --> 20:11.840
I heard you got to F-rank!

20:11.840 --> 20:13.500
Looks like you're doing well!

20:17.060 --> 20:19.590
You're a cutie, mister.

20:21.220 --> 20:24.120
Doc, that medicine really worked!

20:30.510 --> 20:32.040
Oh, Curran!

20:32.040 --> 20:33.900
Come over and let's have a drink!

20:33.900 --> 20:36.570
Sure! Let's have another drinking party!

20:37.300 --> 20:38.920
It's kinda loud.

20:39.320 --> 20:40.120
Yes...

20:41.330 --> 20:43.640
Miss, come on an adventure with me!

20:43.640 --> 20:45.060
I-I'm in love with you!

20:45.060 --> 20:46.390
Be my girlfriend, please!

20:47.370 --> 20:49.250
Why's it so busy?

20:50.410 --> 20:52.880
And what are you doing here?

20:56.890 --> 20:58.020
<i>It's strange...</i>

20:58.670 --> 21:03.870
<i>I never could've imagined the first time I
sat down here that I'd feel so at peace.</i>

21:05.080 --> 21:06.800
<i>It's so warm...</i>

21:07.300 --> 21:10.230
<i>It was probably like this on that day.</i>

21:44.330 --> 21:46.020
Um...

21:46.850 --> 21:49.130
Can we have a little talk?

21:50.510 --> 21:53.550
Search the Labyrinth of Bonds?

21:54.500 --> 21:55.750
What's that?

21:55.960 --> 21:59.160
There's something I want you to find for me.

21:59.160 --> 22:01.240
Don't keep us waiting. What is it?

22:01.930 --> 22:05.120
The sacred blade, "the Sword of Bonds".

22:06.470 --> 22:11.260
<i>Now, whether they took this job or not</i>

22:11.260 --> 22:15.190
<i>would determine their fates
for the rest of their lives...</i>

23:36.320 --> 23:39.020
Next time: "The Labyrinth of Bonds".

23:36.320 --> 23:39.980
<b>Next time:
"The Labyrinth of Bonds"</b>
